  "text": {
    "markdown": "## New York → Lisbon: six flights\n\nI cannot give you live filters in a text reply, so here are the flights sorted by price, the answers to the most likely filters, and what to tell me to narrow it down.\n\n| Flight | Airline | Stops | Departs | Price |\n| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| IB6252 | Iberia | 1 stop | 21:40 | **$480** |\n| DL272 | Delta | 1 stop | 16:05 | $520 |\n| AF11 | Air France | 1 stop | 19:00 | $560 |\n| TP210 | TAP | Nonstop | 22:55 | $590 |\n| TP202 | TAP | Nonstop | 18:30 | $640 |\n| UA64 | United | Nonstop | 20:15 | $710 |\n\n### Common filters, already applied\n\n- **Cheapest overall:** Iberia IB6252, $480 (1 stop, 21:40).\n- **Cheapest nonstop:** TAP TP210, $590 (22:55). Going nonstop costs at least $110 more than the cheapest option.\n- **Nonstop only:** TP210 $590 · TP202 $640 · UA64 $710.\n- **Under $550:** IB6252 $480 · DL272 $520 (both 1 stop).\n- **Under $600:** adds AF11 $560 and TP210 $590, which is the only nonstop at that price.\n- **Earliest departure:** Delta DL272 at 16:05. **Latest:** TAP TP210 at 22:55.\n- **By airline:** TAP has two flights, both nonstop. United is nonstop only. Delta, Iberia and Air France each have one flight with one stop.\n\n### My pick\n\nIf you want nonstop, **TAP TP210 at $590** is the best value, as long as a 22:55 departure works. If you would rather leave earlier, **TAP TP202 at 18:30** is $50 more. If price is all that matters, **Iberia IB6252 at $480**.\n\n### To narrow it down, tell me\n\n1. Your **maximum price**\n2. **Nonstop only**, or is one stop fine?\n3. Any **airlines** to include or avoid\n4. Which flight you want, and I will pick it for you\n",
